# `opencode.jsonc` — the harness config in one file

## What this file is

Your assistant's harness config. It declares the **model**, **agents**,
**permissions**, **MCP servers**, and more. Structure first, tools second — every
harness has an equivalent.

## Generic (vendor-neutral) — what a harness config usually declares

```jsonc
{
  "model": "<default model>",
  "smallModel": "<cheap model for summaries>",
  "instructions": ["AGENTS.md"],
  "permissions": { "read": "allow", "write": "ask", "shell": "ask" },
  "agents": { "<name>": { "description": "...", "tools": ["..."] } }
}
```

## opencode-specific — `opencode.jsonc` (copy this)

```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",

  // Models: a capable default + a cheap one for titles/summaries.
  "model": "openrouter/<vendor>/<model-id>",
  "small_model": "openrouter/<vendor>/<small-model-id>",

  // Start read-only; switch to build when ready.
  "default_agent": "plan",

  // Standing instructions loaded every session.
  "instructions": ["AGENTS.md", "examples/01-instructions/rules/frontend.md"],

  // Permissions: allow reads, ask for writes/network, deny the dangerous stuff.
  "permission": {
    "read": { "*": "allow", "*.env": "deny", "*.env.example": "allow" },
    "edit": "allow",
    "bash": {
      "*": "ask",
      "ls*": "allow", "cat*": "allow", "rg *": "allow", "git status*": "allow",
      "npm run lint*": "allow", "npm run build*": "allow",
      "git push*": "deny", "rm -rf *": "deny", "sudo *": "deny"
    },
    "external_directory": "ask"
  },

  // A focused subagent (see examples/05-agents/reviewer.agent.md).
  "agent": {
    "reviewer": { "mode": "subagent", "description": "Reviews diffs for bugs and style." }
  },

  // Slash commands live as markdown in .opencode/command/*.md
  "command": {
    "test": { "description": "Run the test suite", "template": "Run the tests and fix failures." }
  },

  // Provider wiring (see providers.openrouter.jsonc).
  "provider": { "openrouter": { "options": { "apiKey": "{env:OPENROUTER_API_KEY}" } } },

  // MCP servers (see examples/03-mcp/mcp.json).
  "mcp": {
    "playwright": { "type": "local", "command": ["npx", "-y", "@playwright/mcp@latest"], "enabled": true }
  }
}
```

> `{env:VAR}` reads from your environment at load time — never hard-code keys.
> Field names are opencode's; confirm against `https://opencode.ai/config.json`.
